  bootwright / cluster sign-on resume
      Restore one managed Ceph cluster's frozen single sign-on: re-prove its CephSignOn and
      cluster, prove from each oauth2-proxy host that the identity provider's discovery
      document answers, re-apply the frozen oauth2-proxy document with the Secrets the apply
      bound, then prove the proxies, enable the dashboard's single sign-on and prove the
      gateway enforces it. Requires a completed apply that realized the cluster's CephSignOn.
      An identity provider that does not answer refuses before anything changes. Repeat an
      interrupted command to finish it; a resume over an active sign-on proves and repairs it.
      Refuses external Ceph. --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright cluster sign-on resume [flags]

  Command flags
      --name  Select the exact object name (required)
      --yes   Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright cluster sign-on resume --context lab --name storage
